        {
          "id": 3032026122,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "I would have wished this patch was not submitted this fast as it does not solve the issue just masks a part of the outcome. More on the point of this, the model and the proxy are not separated as they should be. That prevents Qt to optimize code on its own. Also, the assumption that the parent never changes only holds true if the functionality never changes for the grouping. Which makes this patch a one way street for the code, requiring major refactoring if we ever want to touch the dialogs again. Sometimes jumping on an issue is too narrow and we should address the underlying architectural issues first before fixing symptoms.",
          "author": {
            "id": 2498449,
            "username": "rknall",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Roland Knall",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
