        {
          "id": 3032097511,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "The model does send the signal to re-evaluate (in tapDraw) and this function could listen for that and recalculate whether there are children for a given QModelIndex only if that has changed, but it still shouldn't do the full mapping that the base QSortFilterProxyModel does just to calculate the number of children every time it receives the resetModel (or LayoutChanged, etc.) signal. At least not so long as the QTreeView displays the model as it's being built, because repeatedly sorting during insertion is incredibly slow, especially for large models.",
